---
description: Apply this rule when the requested change is medium or large and needs formal spec gating.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

- Trigger OpenSpec when the change adds a feature, touches API/schema/contract/auth/security, spans more than 3 production files, or is expected to take more than 45 minutes.
- Explicitly use `openspec-context-loading` before drafting or modifying a proposal.
- Explicitly use `openspec-proposal-creation` to create or update `spec/changes/<change-id>/proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and spec deltas.
- Make the OpenSpec proposal detailed enough that the primary assistant could implement it directly if the execution role later moves back to the strong model.
- Once the proposal is approved, hand execution to the secondary assistant and set the workflow owner to `secondary_execute`.
